    "body": "## Complete analytic joint law, in explicit-transform form\n\nGives the finite-k joint Laplace transform of the Brownian first-visit cell lengths for both starting-position models in the full original source: independent uniform seeds and equidistant seeds. Every coefficient is a finite sum of deterministic finite-dimensional integrals of explicit one-dimensional exit kernels, over linear inequalities comparing cumulative physical hitting times. A uniform factorial bound controls truncation of the outer series, and compact-support moment determinacy identifies the full joint probability measure.\n\nThe walkers continue independently through previous targets, other starting points and encounters. The proof treats the singleton-target two-endpoint kernel and the spatial null sets of ties and repeated queries explicitly.\n\nSeparate adversarial AI review passed without correction. The proof is unchanged from the reviewed snapshot. All 8,520 submitted exact controls reproduce byte-identically, and 46,056 independent controls pass. Eight independent review files are included.\n\nThis answers the distribution request in the stated explicit-transform sense. It does not claim a simple named density, efficient numerical quadrature, historical priority, or human peer review. The classical Brownian kernels and strong Markov property are credited. One substantive approach family is recorded (1/5). The coordinating task owns the claimed_solved queue update.\n\nMain artifact: `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003818/JOINT_LAW.md`\nReview: `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003818/review/REVIEW.md`\n",
